where people willingly risked
their lives on the daily

01:13:15.470 --> 01:13:20.240
by taking a motorcycle taxi daily

01:13:20.240 --> 01:13:22.870
in some of the most
dangerous roads in the world

01:13:22.870 --> 01:13:25.860
just to save yourself
30 minutes of traffic.

01:13:25.860 --> 01:13:28.130
And we do that on a daily
and I do that on a daily.

01:13:28.130 --> 01:13:31.263
I'm just like, that's weird
when you think about it.

01:13:31.263 --> 01:13:32.490
- I can't really describe

01:13:32.490 --> 01:13:34.490
why I just wanted to take the elevator.

01:13:34.490 --> 01:13:36.210
But I think I just realized,

01:13:36.210 --> 01:13:39.120
I could either walk
down 70 floors of stairs

01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:42.050
or I could just risk it
and take the elevator.

01:13:42.050 --> 01:13:44.350
And I think at that point in time, to me,

01:13:44.350 --> 01:13:47.648
taking 70 flights of stairs
was not worth my life.

01:13:47.648 --> 01:13:49.770
- Well, I mean, I can't argue against that

01:13:49.770 --> 01:13:51.378
'cause I also went in the elevator.

01:13:51.378 --> 01:13:53.840
(laughs)

01:13:53.840 --> 01:13:55.565
- I think it was one of those
things where it was like,

01:13:55.565 --> 01:13:58.016
Connor's going in the elevator.

01:13:58.016 --> 01:13:59.640
All right if he's stupid
enough to risk his life,

01:13:59.640 --> 01:14:02.100
I guess I feel confident enough
where I'll go in with it.

01:14:02.100 --> 01:14:03.930
I can blame Connor if I die.

01:14:03.930 --> 01:14:04.763
- Yeah, exactly.

01:14:04.763 --> 01:14:07.300
- I don't know, I know that
I shouldn't do it, but I did.

01:14:07.300 --> 01:14:09.390
- I mean, we ended up
not going down anyway.

01:14:09.390 --> 01:14:11.380
- Yeah, so what ended up
happening was cosmic justice,

01:14:11.380 --> 01:14:12.810
is that the elevator to get down,

01:14:12.810 --> 01:14:14.864
you had to go up to the
70th floor, to the lobby,

01:14:14.864 --> 01:14:17.780
to then get down and when
we got to the 70th floor,

01:14:17.780 --> 01:14:19.000
they stopped all the elevators.

01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:21.607
- So basically, we went down
about 35 stairs for nothing.

01:14:21.607 --> 01:14:23.221
So basically just instant karma.

01:14:23.221 --> 01:14:25.580
- Instant karma compilation.

01:14:25.580 --> 01:14:27.440
- And then we waited 10 minutes

01:14:27.440 --> 01:14:28.890
and the elevator started working.

01:14:28.890 --> 01:14:29.980
- Yeah, and then there was no problems.

01:14:29.980 --> 01:14:31.190
- And I was very delighted by it.

01:14:31.190 --> 01:14:32.700
- [Navi] I literally
looked back and was like,

01:14:32.700 --> 01:14:33.995
where the fuck are they?

01:14:33.995 --> 01:14:36.050
- Meanwhile, Navi was like,
went down 70 flights of stairs,

01:14:36.050 --> 01:14:37.240
turned around, was like.

01:14:37.240 --> 01:14:40.310
- But you know, when
stuff like that happens,

01:14:40.310 --> 01:14:43.330
I feel like I don't wanna
be that guy who's panicking

01:14:43.330 --> 01:14:44.244
and running around like all these people.

01:14:44.244 --> 01:14:46.170
- No that's the worst thing to do.

01:14:46.170 --> 01:14:48.220
I just feel like this is.
- Dopey sheep.

01:14:49.520 --> 01:14:50.370
- Wake up sheeple.

01:14:50.370 --> 01:14:53.533
- This is how you're inviting
a shitty situation to happen.

01:14:54.923 --> 01:14:58.750
You know, I also don't wanna
try my chances on the road.

01:14:58.750 --> 01:15:00.023
'Cause when you leave the hotel,

01:15:00.023 --> 01:15:01.566
you're just facing the road.

01:15:01.566 --> 01:15:03.830
I don't want to try my
chance with stuff falling

01:15:03.830 --> 01:15:06.813
or people driving on the
road in an earthquake.

01:15:06.813 --> 01:15:09.410
I was pretty content
that my room was fine.

01:15:09.410 --> 01:15:10.243
I was like, oh whatever.

01:15:10.243 --> 01:15:11.840
- Well, that's the
thing, in some situations

01:15:11.840 --> 01:15:13.360
it's actually more dangerous
to go out on the road

01:15:13.360 --> 01:15:14.970
because in the case with Japan,

01:15:14.970 --> 01:15:17.220
we have so much like electrical
wiring from the roads

01:15:17.220 --> 01:15:20.130
that if those fall and snap,
they can easily electrocute you

01:15:20.130 --> 01:15:23.860
fucking traffic signs
can come down, hurt you.

01:15:23.860 --> 01:15:26.800
- I feel like the safest
place is just to probably be

01:15:26.800 --> 01:15:28.110
on the ground floor.

01:15:28.110 --> 01:15:29.105
- Yes.
- Of a building.

01:15:29.105 --> 01:15:32.350
- I dunno but you get way more
like earthquake vibrations

01:15:32.350 --> 01:15:33.880
on the first floor.
- Do you?

01:15:33.880 --> 01:15:36.510
- Yeah, the higher up the
building, the less you get.

01:15:36.510 --> 01:15:38.680
You just get swaying if you're up top.

01:15:38.680 --> 01:15:39.970
And when you're down below

01:15:39.970 --> 01:15:41.560
you get the fucking violent shaking.

01:15:41.560 --> 01:15:43.670
- Yeah, the best thing
to do is to just go out

01:15:43.670 --> 01:15:45.457
into like a really, really open field.

01:15:45.457 --> 01:15:47.210
- I feel like this is a point in my life

01:15:47.210 --> 01:15:48.043
where I'm just like,

01:15:48.043 --> 01:15:49.795
I don't know if I should
listen to this advice.

01:15:49.795 --> 01:15:53.320
- Well, 'cause the really tall buildings

01:15:53.320 --> 01:15:55.323
are built on like rolling mechanics.

01:15:56.460 --> 01:15:59.370
So when the building, you
fucking experienced it.

01:15:59.370 --> 01:16:00.203
- What'd you mean?

01:16:00.203 --> 01:16:01.720
- The hotel we stayed in?

01:16:01.720 --> 01:16:02.553
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:16:02.553 --> 01:16:04.820
- It's built on rollers so that
when the earthquake happens,

01:16:04.820 --> 01:16:05.760
it starts rolling.

01:16:05.760 --> 01:16:08.150
- Yeah, but on the ground floor.

01:16:08.150 --> 01:16:10.210
Sometimes you literally don't
even feel the earthquake.

01:16:10.210 --> 01:16:12.710
Because there's no swaying
or anything like that.

01:16:12.710 --> 01:16:13.860
- No, 'cause you're getting like

01:16:13.860 --> 01:16:15.940
the actual fucking earth shaking.

01:16:15.940 --> 01:16:18.720
- That's not what it feels
like on the ground floor.

01:16:18.720 --> 01:16:20.331
- Yeah, it does!

01:16:20.331 --> 01:16:21.797
- You've had an earthquake
on the ground floor, right?

01:16:21.797 --> 01:16:22.630
- Yeah.

01:16:22.630 --> 01:16:24.140
- It feels very violently shaking.

01:16:24.140 --> 01:16:27.373
- Yeah, but it's kind of the
same as being on the building.

01:16:27.373 --> 01:16:29.710
- When I experienced both in Japan,

01:16:29.710 --> 01:16:31.690
I definitely prefer in LA

01:16:31.690 --> 01:16:33.580
when the building was just swaying.

01:16:33.580 --> 01:16:34.538
I liked that a lot more.

01:16:34.538 --> 01:16:35.480
- I was literally on the street

01:16:35.480 --> 01:16:37.340
and sometimes I didn't even notice

01:16:37.340 --> 01:16:39.180
that there was an
earthquake when people will.

01:16:39.180 --> 01:16:40.602
- What?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:16:40.602 --> 01:16:45.130
'Cause there's nothing to
like, how can I put this?

01:16:45.130 --> 01:16:46.760
There's nothing to put your perspective

01:16:46.760 --> 01:16:47.980
in that you're in an earthquake.

01:16:47.980 --> 01:16:50.420
You just feel a bit wobbly.
- The floor is moving.

01:16:50.420 --> 01:16:53.520
- The floor doesn't move, it shakes.

01:16:53.520 --> 01:16:54.353
- Does it?

01:16:54.353 --> 01:16:55.944
- It shakes but a lot of the times

01:16:55.944 --> 01:16:56.980
you can't actually see it moving

01:16:56.980 --> 01:16:57.930
until you look at something.

01:16:57.930 --> 01:17:01.400
- Yeah, there's nothing to
ground your perspective.

01:17:01.400 --> 01:17:02.530
- Whereas, if you're in a building,

01:17:02.530 --> 01:17:04.110
you can see other buildings doing this.

01:17:04.110 --> 01:17:04.943
- Yeah, yeah, exactly.

01:17:04.943 --> 01:17:06.207
- I don't really mind though.

01:17:06.207 --> 01:17:08.330
Most of the times, I don't even
realize I'm in an earthquake

01:17:08.330 --> 01:17:11.500
until I have something to
like ground that perspective.

01:17:11.500 --> 01:17:14.009
Sometime like living in Japan,

01:17:14.009 --> 01:17:16.050
sometimes I just get up, get a head rush,

01:17:16.050 --> 01:17:18.332
I'm like, ooh, was that an earthquake?

01:17:18.332 --> 01:17:19.165
- Like do you ever get that?

01:17:19.165 --> 01:17:21.110
- Yeah, but because there's
so many light earthquakes.

01:17:21.110 --> 01:17:23.050
But you know when you're
getting an earthquake,

01:17:23.050 --> 01:17:24.947
'cause it used to be like, just fucking.

01:17:24.947 --> 01:17:27.350
- My mom has this story
of when she was in school,

01:17:27.350 --> 01:17:29.950
she was like running along
the tracks at school.

01:17:29.950 --> 01:17:31.610
And you know when you're running,

01:17:31.610 --> 01:17:33.340
your entire world is doing this.

01:17:33.340 --> 01:17:34.390
So she was running and she was looking

01:17:34.390 --> 01:17:36.469
at the school building
and then she stopped

01:17:36.469 --> 01:17:37.437
and the building just kept doing this

01:17:37.437 --> 01:17:39.217
and she realized she was in an earthquake.

01:17:39.217 --> 01:17:41.200
And she didn't realize until she stopped

01:17:41.200 --> 01:17:43.990
because to her perspective,
it's already going up and down.

01:17:43.990 --> 01:17:47.010
But then, I think again,
it's that like perspective

01:17:47.010 --> 01:17:50.794
of being, that's not moving
the way it's intended to.

01:17:50.794 --> 01:17:53.900
- But also, the swaying
and all that stuff,

01:17:53.900 --> 01:17:54.733
I don't really give a shit,

01:17:54.733 --> 01:17:57.850
as long as the building
isn't falling down.

01:17:57.850 --> 01:17:58.683
- Yeah.

01:17:58.683 --> 01:18:00.350
- And I just don't want my stuff to break.

01:18:00.350 --> 01:18:02.013
- Well, yeah, that's the biggest thing

01:18:02.013 --> 01:18:03.243
is just shit falling down, isn't it?

01:18:03.243 --> 01:18:05.639
- Yeah, that's why if I ever
knew there was an earthquake,

01:18:05.639 --> 01:18:06.710
I would just rush to my like camera gear.

01:18:06.710 --> 01:18:08.589
I'm like hold my shirt and coat.

01:18:08.589 --> 01:18:09.800
- Protect, protect.

01:18:09.800 --> 01:18:10.657
- JoJo figures, please.

01:18:10.657 --> 01:18:11.870
- Me and my anime figures.

01:18:11.870 --> 01:18:12.703
- No, no!

01:18:14.122 --> 01:18:15.350
- Those are the real
casualties in earthquakes.

01:18:15.350 --> 01:18:18.190
- I had those 400, $500 Jojo figures

01:18:18.190 --> 01:18:20.220
that were like very finely balanced.

01:18:20.220 --> 01:18:23.523
That were balanced, the
weight was like this.

01:18:23.523 --> 01:18:26.580
So that the center of
gravity was very worrying.

01:18:26.580 --> 01:18:27.413
And during earthquakes,

01:18:27.413 --> 01:18:30.081
I immediately had to just like
go to them if I was there.

01:18:30.081 --> 01:18:31.740
And during, we had one
pretty big earthquake

01:18:31.740 --> 01:18:33.900
and I was surprised 'cause
my figures just stayed up.

01:18:33.900 --> 01:18:35.487
- Well, I mean same
with the studio as well.

01:18:35.487 --> 01:18:36.320
- Yeah, yours didn't.

01:18:36.320 --> 01:18:37.476
- Yeah.

01:18:37.476 --> 01:18:39.560
- It's weird 'cause the
figures that had fallen

01:18:39.560 --> 01:18:41.073
looked like pretty normal figures

01:18:41.073 --> 01:18:43.550
but the one that I really expect to break,

01:18:43.550 --> 01:18:44.470
didn't move at all.

01:18:44.470 --> 01:18:45.840
- Well, I mean, it's
the same here as well.

01:18:45.840 --> 01:18:47.120
Like at the old track station.

01:18:47.120 --> 01:18:49.300
- I expected Rohan to just be over.

01:18:49.300 --> 01:18:52.330
- All of these knockedover,
but the only casualty we had

01:18:52.330 --> 01:18:53.240
was fucking Mike.

01:18:53.240 --> 01:18:54.720
- Fucking Mike.

01:18:54.720 --> 01:18:56.048
- Every time I'm not at my house

01:18:56.048 --> 01:18:56.913
and there's an earthquake in Japan,

01:18:56.913 --> 01:18:59.040
I just assume my house
is gonna be demolished

01:18:59.040 --> 01:18:59.890
when I'm back.

01:18:59.890 --> 01:19:01.220
I'm like, everything's fucked,

01:19:01.220 --> 01:19:03.300
I have to rebuild my whole
life, it's all ruined.

01:19:03.300 --> 01:19:05.820
- Do you guys have like the
anti-earthquake proof stuff

01:19:05.820 --> 01:19:06.653
in your cabinets?

01:19:06.653 --> 01:19:07.486
- No.

01:19:07.486 --> 01:19:08.319
- You probably should do that.

01:19:08.319 --> 01:19:09.152
- No.

01:19:09.152 --> 01:19:09.985
- It really does make a difference.

01:19:09.985 --> 01:19:10.818
- Does it?

01:19:10.818 --> 01:19:11.651
- Yeah.
- What is it?

01:19:11.651 --> 01:19:12.484
- So basically like,

01:19:12.484 --> 01:19:13.317
or, I mean there's lots of
different variations of it.

01:19:13.317 --> 01:19:14.950
- Do you need it for most stuff though?

01:19:14.950 --> 01:19:17.050
I feel like it's for very specific things.

01:19:18.000 --> 01:19:19.010
- We put it on most stuff.

01:19:19.010 --> 01:19:20.300
Like most of the big
stuff will sound like,

01:19:20.300 --> 01:19:22.700
if you have figuring
cabinets or like bookshelves,

01:19:22.700 --> 01:19:23.930
this is like little, kind of like,

01:19:23.930 --> 01:19:25.730
they look like little rubber doorstoppers.

01:19:25.730 --> 01:19:26.927
- Yeah, I know what they
are, I know what they are.

01:19:26.927 --> 01:19:28.890
- And you put them underneath
and it completely stops

01:19:28.890 --> 01:19:29.750
the shaking from happening.

01:19:29.750 --> 01:19:32.020
- I wanted to get the
figures to stop shaking.

01:19:32.020 --> 01:19:35.030
- Yes I have them under
like all of my bookshelves

01:19:35.030 --> 01:19:35.863
and figuring cabinets and stuff like that.

01:19:35.863 --> 01:19:38.970
And you know, I've seen
the move in an earthquake.

01:19:38.970 --> 01:19:40.170
That shit doesn't budge.

01:19:40.170 --> 01:19:41.380
So that's really good.

01:19:41.380 --> 01:19:44.290
And also like there's also
these little sticky pads

01:19:44.290 --> 01:19:46.570
kind of thing that you
can put on some figurines

01:19:46.570 --> 01:19:47.733
and stuff like that stops
them from falling over.

01:19:47.733 --> 01:19:48.566
- It's just weird that you
have to live in a country

01:19:48.566 --> 01:19:52.250
and you can just worry
about like instant death

01:19:52.250 --> 01:19:53.410
just happening.

01:19:53.410 --> 01:19:54.903
In the UK nothing kills you.

01:19:54.903 --> 01:19:57.190
- Instant death, I mean
it;snot exactly instant death

01:19:57.190 --> 01:19:59.561
- I was just worried,
well, I mean, it might be.

01:19:59.561 --> 01:20:00.730
- If you're in the wrong situation.

01:20:00.730 --> 01:20:02.230
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:20:02.230 --> 01:20:03.820
- I suppose we've been lucky enough

01:20:03.820 --> 01:20:07.094
to had never have been
in a bad earthquake.

01:20:07.094 --> 01:20:09.345
I don't know, I feel like we've never.

01:20:09.345 --> 01:20:10.690
- Garnt says this, don't fucking say it.

01:20:10.690 --> 01:20:13.029
Well they've been
predicting the mega-quake

01:20:13.029 --> 01:20:14.587
for a few years now in Tokyo.

01:20:14.587 --> 01:20:16.380
Where there's bound to be some kind of

01:20:16.380 --> 01:20:20.150
magnitude eight or nine
fucking earthquake in Tokyo

01:20:20.150 --> 01:20:23.030
and I hope to God it happens
in the next three weeks

01:20:23.030 --> 01:20:23.863
so I'm not here.

01:20:23.863 --> 01:20:25.560
(laughs)

01:20:25.560 --> 01:20:26.393
- Jesus Christ.

01:20:26.393 --> 01:20:27.226
- I bet you'll wish you were

01:20:27.226 --> 01:20:28.059
on the ground floor then, Connor.

01:20:28.059 --> 01:20:29.241
- Yeah, exactly.

01:20:29.241 --> 01:20:31.500
- Well, I felt like the
shaking was very violent.

01:20:31.500 --> 01:20:33.990
I used to live on the 4 to 5th floor

01:20:33.990 --> 01:20:36.810
and it used to shake really
weirdly, I didn't like it.

01:20:36.810 --> 01:20:37.760
I felt like it was just high enough up

01:20:37.760 --> 01:20:39.620
where I got really violent shakes.

01:20:39.620 --> 01:20:40.453
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:20:40.453 --> 01:20:42.130
- Yeah, I got, I was on the 8th floor,

01:20:42.130 --> 01:20:44.921
and I think with the biggest
earthcake we were in,

01:20:44.921 --> 01:20:46.356
which was the one where,
- Earthcake.

01:20:46.356 --> 01:20:49.000
- Earthcake, earthquake,
(laughs) earthcake.

01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:50.144
The biggest earthquake we were in,

01:20:50.144 --> 01:20:51.617
which was the one where
my figures fell over,

01:20:51.617 --> 01:20:54.540
I was in the toilet at the time, but.

01:20:54.540 --> 01:20:55.620
- That's the safest room to be in.

01:20:55.620 --> 01:20:57.506
- I was in the bath one time as well.

01:20:57.506 --> 01:21:00.304
- But that earthquake just
lasted for so fucking long.

01:21:00.304 --> 01:21:02.410
It felt like it lasted like two minutes

01:21:02.410 --> 01:21:03.750
or something like that.
- At least, yeah.

01:21:03.750 --> 01:21:04.583
- Yeah, go on.

01:21:04.583 --> 01:21:07.360
- Yeah, 'cause it just started
and like at which point,

01:21:07.360 --> 01:21:09.690
'cause you have to make
this mental judgment of,

01:21:09.690 --> 01:21:11.730
at which point do I start giving a shit?

01:21:11.730 --> 01:21:12.669
- Yeah, yeah.

01:21:12.669 --> 01:21:13.520
(laughs)

01:21:13.520 --> 01:21:15.603
Yeah, because most of the
time it's a little shake.

01:21:15.603 --> 01:21:16.436
- 'Cause it happens so often.

01:21:16.436 --> 01:21:17.527
- It happens so often, so I'm just like,

01:21:17.527 --> 01:21:19.574
uh, is this the one I should start caring.

01:21:19.574 --> 01:21:21.133
It's not stopping, should
I start caring now?

01:21:21.133 --> 01:21:23.960
- But also, what are you
gonna do if you give a shit?

01:21:23.960 --> 01:21:24.970
Like, what am I gonna do?

01:21:24.970 --> 01:21:26.750
Just be like, oh shit, I'm worried.

01:21:26.750 --> 01:21:27.980
- Well, you have to like evacuate

01:21:27.980 --> 01:21:29.380
to your nearest evacuation point,

01:21:29.380 --> 01:21:31.300
which everyone should know when you move.

01:21:31.300 --> 01:21:32.540
Do you know where is it?

01:21:32.540 --> 01:21:33.373
- Fuck no.

01:21:33.373 --> 01:21:34.496
(laughs)

01:21:34.496 --> 01:21:36.750
- You gotta get under
the doorframe, right?

01:21:36.750 --> 01:21:38.570
- Doorframe, but also like
if it gets really bad,

01:21:38.570 --> 01:21:40.410
then there's like in your local town,

01:21:40.410 --> 01:21:41.890
there's usually like evacuation points

01:21:41.890 --> 01:21:42.826
that you have to go to.

01:21:42.826 --> 01:21:44.690
- That's normally if your
water and shit turns off

01:21:44.690 --> 01:21:45.523
and all that, is right?

01:21:45.523 --> 01:21:48.070
- No, in a lot of situations
it's like earthquakes

01:21:48.070 --> 01:21:49.557
and floods and stuff like that, yeah.

01:21:49.557 --> 01:21:51.690
